    "codeLanguage": "javascript",
    "title": "What is JSON",
    "descriptionContent": "Learn about JSON and why they are useful for front-end developers.",
    "shortDescriptionContent": "",
    "showInTrack": true,
    "iconBanner": null,
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": 17523,
        "title": "A JSON in JS",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 148616,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You already know what a JS object is. Let's now get to know what JSON is. JSON stands for <strong>JavaScript Object Notation</strong>.</p><p>In games, we can use this data format to store and exchange things like player stats, save files, and level data.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 148617,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>JSON looks like a <em>stringified</em> version of a regular JS object.</p><p>We can create <code>jsonLevelData</code> like a regular object <code>{}</code> but wrapped with single quotes <code>'</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"22\" endIndex=\"23\" /><option startIndex=\"23\" endIndex=\"24\" /><option startIndex=\"24\" endIndex=\"25\" /><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"26\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" jsonLevelData = \" /><text value=\"'{}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>'</code> followed by <code>{</code> and then <code>}</code>, <code>'</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 148618,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A JSON object contains a collection of key-value pairs, similar to a JS object.</p><p>However, in a JSON, we need to include the keys between quotes, like <code>\"score\"</code> here.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"41\" endIndex=\"42\" /><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"47\" /><option startIndex=\"47\" endIndex=\"48\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" jsonString = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;player&quot;: &quot;Ranger&quot;, &quot;score&quot;: 200, &quot;alive&quot;: true }'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>\"</code>, followed by <code>score</code>, and finally <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 148619,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>JSON objects can gather static data like Numbers, Arrays, Booleans, or Strings. However, they <strong>cannot</strong> store functions inside.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"function(){}\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"60\" endIndex=\"64\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" saveFile = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;player&quot;: &quot;Ranger&quot;,&quot;score&quot;: 200,&quot;alive&quot;: true}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>true</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 148620,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the following data type?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" player = {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"inventory\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": [\" /><text value=\"&quot;potion&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;sword&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;shield&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"],\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"health\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A JS object</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">A JSON</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A JS object.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 148621,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can convert a JS object to a JSON with the <code>JSON.stringify()</code> method.</p><p>Here we can convert the <code>enemy</code> JS object into a JSON string if we use <code>JSON.stringify(enemy)</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"75\" endIndex=\"79\" /><option startIndex=\"80\" endIndex=\"89\" /><option startIndex=\"90\" endIndex=\"95\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemy = {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"type\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"&quot;Slime&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\",\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"hp\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemy);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".stringify(enemy));\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>JSON</code>, followed by <code>stringify</code>, and finally <code>enemy</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 148622,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can also transform a JSON string into a JS object with the <code>JSON.parse()</code> method.</p><p>If we include <code>playerSave</code> in the parentheses, we'll transform the JSON string into a JS object.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"60\" endIndex=\"64\" /><option startIndex=\"65\" endIndex=\"70\" /><option startIndex=\"71\" endIndex=\"81\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerSave = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Nova&quot;,&quot;level&quot;:3}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".parse(playerSave));\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>JSON</code>, followed by <code>parse</code>, and finally <code>playerSave</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 148623,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How can we convert a JS object into a JSON string?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">With <code>JSON.stringify</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">With <code>JSON.parse</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">With <code>JSON.stringify</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 148624,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What will the console display?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" gameState = {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"score\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"13\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\",\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"paused\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"false\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".stringify(gameState));\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>{\"score\": 13, \"paused\": false}</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>{score: 13, paused : false}</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>{\"score\": 13, \"paused\": false}</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 148625,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Complete the following JSON.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"21\" /><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"26\" /><option startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"57\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" levelInfo = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Forest-1&quot;, &quot;enemies&quot;: 123 }'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>'</code> followed by <code>\"</code> and then <code>\"</code>, <code>'</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 148626,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>*<em>Parse</em> the <code>saveData</code> JSON string so that we see a JS object in the console output.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"88\" endIndex=\"93\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" saveData = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;player&quot;: &quot;Nova&quot;, &quot;checkpoint&quot;:&quot;Cave&quot;}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" parsedSaveData = \" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".parse(saveData);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(parsedSaveData);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>parse</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}